I forget.  I might have quafed a potion or two to have upped it
somewhat, but probably not too many.  IIRC, most of the denizens
of minetown were either friendly or wimps, and from that moment
on, my highest priority was to level up; knocking out the wimps
helped that (and my luck, as I was sacrificing them).

But again, it's not something that I'd consider a typical
situation, and not something I target.  It just happened that
way, and the RGN was obviously being friendly: minetown at the
highest possible level, all intermediate levels lit, lots of
good armor very early, vaults and a few gems---with that sort of
help, the protection racket can work.  Curiously enough, I did
the same thing a second time just a couple of days ago.  The
game following that one was just the opposite, however---my pet
staunchly refused to kill anything, minetown was at level 8,
with all intermediate levels dark, no vaults or gems, etc. So I
ended up leveling up fairly quickly, and not buying protection
until much, much later.  It also worked, or was working, until I
choked on my food.

